WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.372
Sometimes blank strings and NULL represent the same business state.

00:00:04.372 --> 00:00:10.152
If that rule is documented, NULLIF can convert a blank-after-trimming string into NULL.

00:00:10.152 --> 00:00:16.377
This can make later logic easier because one missing representation is easier to handle than several.

00:00:16.377 --> 00:00:20.417
But do this only when blank truly means missing for that field.

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:25.382
Missingness has several representations: NULL, blank text, whitespace,

00:00:25.382 --> 00:00:28.012
and sometimes sentinel codes such as Unknown or 999.

00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:30.612
Do not collapse them blindly.

00:00:30.612 --> 00:00:36.247
First decide whether they mean the same thing in the source system,

00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:40.960
then normalize deliberately and keep lineage when the original value may matter.
